            <ArticleTitle>Indwelling ureteral stents: impact of material and shape on patient comfort.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Indwelling ureteral stents are essential in urology today. No ideal stent has been designed. The principal sources of discomfort are a long intravesical segment, inefficient drainage, displacement, and stiffness. Discomfort may be a small price to pay for the overall benefit to the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
